practice_explanation = "Merge Sort always runs in O(n log n) regardless of input. Each level does O(n) work for merging, and there are log n levels because the array splits in half each time. Unlike Quick Sort, it NEVER degrades to O(n²). The trade-off is the O(n) extra memory it needs."
